lience, communication, cooperation.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but makes nasty remarks, sometimes wrong tone. Strengths: reliability, stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). Concerns: communication, teamwork.\n\nCandidate C: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, understands complicated technology, excellent attention. Strengths: decision quality, technical competence, attention. Concerns: communication, egocentric, lack of development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, has hot temper, regarded as loner. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: hot temper, loner (cooperation).\n\nWe need to pick best overall. Likely B has strong reliability and stress, but communication issues. D has responsibility but temper. C has decision and technical but egocentric. A has anticipation and leadership but not open to new ideas.\n\nProbably B is strong on reliability and stress, but communication issues could be serious for crew cooperation. D's hot temper also problematic. C's egocentric also problematic. A's lack of openness may affect adaptability.\n\nThus maybe B is best despite communication concerns, but we need to discuss. As first contribution, we can propose provisional recommendation for Candidate B, citing strengths and concerns, and note need to discuss communication further.\n\nLet's produce public message."}
